{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pulls/20","id":4804164673,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVB5edM8AAAABHlm8QQ","html_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pull/20","diff_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pull/20.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pull/20.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/issues/20","number":20,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Specify the entity in YAML and generate the cores' C configuration","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[A580]\n\nRelates to #2\n\nDescribe one entity in versioned YAML and generate const ADP, ACMP and MAAP configuration. Derive shared identity, MACs, counts and interface mappings together. Refuse invalid fields before writing output.\n\nAdds listener, talker, duplex and AX7101 examples, byte-equal golden checks, and round trips through all three cores on both targets. The [schema and firmware mapping](docs/ENTITY_YAML.md) document field ranges, clauses and integration.\n\n## Round 2\n\nPreserve the source schema's quoted hexadecimal values, including digit-only identities. Check prefixes, underscores, widths, types and resolved declarations. Apply the builder defaults for omitted `vendor_name`, `group_name` and `entity_id`, and normalize supported MAC forms. Record ENTITY-01 with its issue-2 origin and reject missing requirement definitions. Clarify YAML quoting and parsed-mapping equality.\n\n## Round 3\n\nAccept the source's optional `entity.firmware_rev`. It must be a non-negative integer and never a boolean; omission means 0. It feeds only the AEM firmware version string, so it sets no core field and the mapped identity is unchanged. The mapper now applies every source entity default: `vendor_name`, `group_name`, `entity_id` and `firmware_rev`.\n\n`entity.firmware_version` stays refused, and its refusal points to `entity.firmware_rev`, as in the source. Every unknown entity key is refused by name, for example `milan.entity.typo: unknown field`. The [mapping table](docs/ENTITY_YAML.md#mapping-from-milan-fpga) has a new row.\n\nThe schema selftest now registers 13 named mapper plants: the eight earlier mapping regressions and five that revert parts of the `firmware_rev` change. Each named test must pass on the unedited mapper and fail an assertion on the planted one. Rerun them alone with:\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/entity_selftest.py --work build-entity-controls --select mapper_plant\n```\n\nThe target check in the requirement records now reads \"requirement must address both targets\".\n\nBoth review probes pass. The source-valid `firmware_rev` values are accepted with an unchanged identity, and `firmware_version` is refused. The 220,328 scalar and MAC differential cases still match the source parsers. All 19 reviewer mapper plants and all 13 registered plants are caught. All 196 schema selftests pass.\n\n## Validate\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/validate.py --work build-validation --jobs 16 --graphs\npython3 scripts/baremetal.py --work build-rv32 --jobs 16\n```\n\nAll 27 Linux gates and both RV32 configurations return zero at the head. All 330 registered C plants are caught by their named assertions. Core line and branch coverage remain 100% after existing exclusions. All four Mermaid graphs render. Core sources, public headers, examples and golden configurations are unchanged in Rounds 2 and 3.\n\nThe integration follow-up issue remains with the manager.\n","created_at":"2026-10-09T18:10:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T20:37:54Z","closed_at":"2026-10-09T20:37:54Z","merged_at":"2026-10-09T20:37:54Z","merge_commit_sha":"98dc9e3076714bebe113982ee18c3c1c496cf3c9","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pulls/20/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pulls/20/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/issues/20/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/statuses/0c5ef532cb782f9e7c73855b41c397679d176ea7","head":{"label":"kebag-logic:entity-yaml","ref":"entity-yaml","sha":"0c5ef532cb782f9e7c73855b41c397679d176ea7","user":{"login":"kebag-logic","id":142733852,"node_id":"O_kgDOCIHyHA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142733852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kebag-logic","html_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kebag-logic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kebag-logic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kebag-logic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kebag-logic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kebag-logic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gi